          <span class="mission-chip">Evolve the value proposition</span>
          <span class="mission-chip">Change ways of working</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="sas-what2-facts">
        <div><dt>1</dt><dd>mission, with a clear goal and end date</dd></div>
        <div><dt>8&ndash;12</dt><dd>of your people, with an executive sponsor</dd></div>
        <div><dt>12&ndash;18</dt><dd>months &mdash; within one leadership tenure</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="sas-more">
      <details class="sas-more-item">
        <summary>What&rsquo;s included</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>A complete strategy deck, built with your core team</li>
          <li>Weekly facilitation through to the finish line</li>
          <li>A visibly more efficient, more aligned team</li>
          <li>Organizational learning that outlasts the original issue</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
      <details class="sas-more-item">
        <summary>Is it a fit for us?</summary>
        <p>We&rsquo;ve applied it at companies from $25M to $2B+ in revenue, and to divisions of much larger ones. It doesn&rsquo;t replace your team &mdash; it adds the outside perspective that brings more commitment and ownership to work already underway.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="sas-more-item">
        <summary>Why 12&ndash;18 months?</summary>
        <p>Twelve months is the minimum for a change that sticks. The more it touches daily habits, not just priorities, the closer it gets to eighteen.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

